914	                                          //   writes the SAME (t,j) — read happens in
915	                                          //   the forward-recompute pass + the
916	                                          //   softplus' uses dt_pre; the WRITE is the
917	                                          //   last op per (t,j). But the recompute
918	                                          //   pass for OTHER t reads dt_pre too. Since
919	                                          //   one thread owns channel j and processes
920	                                          //   ALL t in its recompute BEFORE the reverse
921	                                          //   pass writes any ddt_pre[*,j], the in-place
922	                                          //   write is safe per channel.)
923	                    &sm->dBmat[0][0], &sm->dCmat[0][0], G.A_log, sm->red);
